133 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 859 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 7 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 219 0 R/Rect[93.6 319.92 799.56 388.56]/T(Proposed Situation_2)/TU(Proposed Situation)/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(- Batch 00004515 stays in quarantine until QA disposition. Proposed route \(QA to decide, see Attachment A, A5\): deviation, with release only if a lot-specific endotoxin test \(QC in-house or approved contract lab, method suitable for this matrix and able to quantify below 1 EU/ml\) gives < 1 EU/ml. Result >= 1 EU/ml = lot rejected. If CompCello's change goes beyond COA reporting, or cannot be confirmed in writing, full requalification applies instead.\n- Revise RMS-3333: keep < 1 EU/ml as an internal acceptance criterion tested on every lot at receipt \(vendor COA value recorded for information\); remove 'only report the results'; correct name 'Antiform' to 'Antifoam'; cap assigned expiry at the manufacturer expiry; add storage 15-30 C.\n- Update the CompCello supplier file / quality agreement and vendor change-notification handling \(see separate Risk Assessment\).)>>
endobj

134 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 861 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 7.5 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 219 0 R/Rect[93.6 234.35999 799.56 303.12]/T(Change Justification_2)/TU(Change Justification)/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(Endotoxin is a critical quality attribute for plasmid DNA products. The vendor no longer certifies a pass/fail endotoxin limit, so the current release basis \(COA against < 1 EU/ml\) cannot be met from the COA, and the reported value \(< 5 EU/ml\) does not rule out levels above the internal limit. Relaxing the RMS limit to 'report only' is not proposed, because no process endotoxin-clearance data has been provided to justify it. Without this change, every future CompCello lot will fail QA review and delay production. The missed vendor notification shows a gap in supplier change-notification handling, which is addressed by the preventive actions in Attachment A \(A7\) and the separate Risk Assessment.)>>
endobj

135 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 857 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 7 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 219 0 R/Rect[93.6 405.36 799.56 474]/T(Current Situation_2)/TU(Current Situation)/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(- RMS-3333 \(issued 12 Apr 2024, QA approved 17 May 2024\) lists Endotoxin Level \(post-irradiation\) with release specification < 1 EU/ml. The test name in the same row also reads 'only report the results', which contradicts the numeric limit.\n- CompCello COA, Prod. 599-12X, Batch 00004515 \(mfd 01 May 2025, QA release 29 May 2025, expiry 01 May 2027\): Endotoxin specification 'Report Result', result '< 5 EU/ml'. A result of < 5 EU/ml does not show compliance with < 1 EU/ml. The other 6 COA tests meet RMS-3333.\n- QA has flagged the lot as non-conforming and a material hold is in place. The lot cannot be used in the upcoming client-critical plasmid GMP run.\n- After the hold, CompCello stated a change notification \(endotoxin moved to 'report only'\) was sent approx. two months ago to an employee who has since left. It was never processed; a copy has been requested.)>>
endobj

